<!-- SECTION: assembly.Assembly — title -->
<div class="titleband" data-screen-label="Assembly — title"><h1>The <span class="u-1">Assembly</span></h1></div>
<div class="introband">
  <h2>A real say — <span class="u-1">advisory first</span>, honest about the limits.</h2>
  <p>The Assembly is how Uncost stays accountable to the people who support it: propose ideas, prioritize work, raise objections, and vote on priorities — with every proposal, method, and aggregate outcome recorded publicly.</p>
</div>
<!-- SECTION: assembly.Status -->
<div class="statusband" data-screen-label="Status">
  <span class="status status--planned">Not yet operational</span>
  <span>No formal vote runs until the governance policy (POL-006) completes independent review, founder review, legal and fiscal-sponsor review where applicable, and formal adoption. At launch, every Assembly outcome is advisory.</span>
</div>

<!-- SECTION: assembly.What supporters can do -->
<section class="u-15 blk blk--cream" data-screen-label="What supporters can do">
  <div class="eyebrow">The participation loop</div>
  <h2 class="u-6 sec">Propose. Deliberate. <span class="u-1">Advise.</span> On the record.</h2>
  <div class="can">
    <div><div class="cn">01</div><h3>Propose</h3><p>Any eligible supporter can raise a proposal. Each gets a public ASM reference, a classification, and a conflict screen.</p></div>
    <div><div class="cn">02</div><h3>Deliberate</h3><p>Published discussion with a balanced record of the arguments for and against — rigorous disagreement is the point.</p></div>
    <div><div class="cn">03</div><h3>Advise</h3><p>Surveys and recorded advisory votes on priorities: which regions or sectors next, which projects, what the public work emphasizes.</p></div>
    <div><div class="cn">04</div><h3>See the record</h3><p>Method, eligibility, aggregate result, turnout, and the action taken — or the documented reason it was declined — all public.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: assembly.Standing rules -->
<section class="blk blk--ink u-block--ink" data-screen-label="Standing rules">
  <div class="u-5 eyebrow">Standing rules</div>
  <h2 class="u-6 sec">Rules that don&rsquo;t <span class="u-1">bend</span>.</h2>
  <div class="rules">
    <div class="rule"><i></i><div><p>One person, one vote.</p><span class="why">Participation is free and never weighted by donations, purchases, assets, or status.</span></div></div>
    <div class="rule"><i></i><div><p>No payment to vote. Donations never buy influence.</p><span class="why">The whole movement opposes wealth determining outcomes — its own governance can&rsquo;t work otherwise.</span></div></div>
    <div class="rule"><i></i><div><p>No tokens, no on-chain voting, no crypto mechanics.</p><span class="why">The Assembly&rsquo;s value is trust and participation, not speculation.</span></div></div>
    <div class="rule"><i></i><div><p>Ballots private, records public.</p><span class="why">Individual ballots stay private; proposals, methods, aggregate outcomes, and follow-up actions are published.</span></div></div>
    <div class="rule"><i></i><div><p>Eligibility comes with The Pledge.</p><span class="why">Signing The Pledge plus a privacy-preserving duplicate check — no biometrics, no government ID assumed.</span></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: assembly.The boundary -->
<section class="blk blk--cream" data-screen-label="The boundary">
  <div class="eyebrow">The honest boundary</div>
  <h2 class="u-16 sec">What the Assembly can — and cannot — decide.</h2>
  <div class="bound">
    <h3>Advisory at launch</h3>
    <p>Every Assembly outcome starts advisory. Where law and governance allow, outcomes may come to determine bounded community priorities — which regions or sectors to focus on next, which community projects to pursue, the direction of public communications — and any such vote is marked <b>subject to legal and fiduciary approval</b>.</p>
    <h3 class="u-17">Reserved matters</h3>
    <p>Finances above set thresholds and legal, fiduciary, safeguarding, privacy, employment, and regulatory duties remain with responsible leadership and the fiscal sponsor. Any binding authority would require legal structure that does not yet exist. Eligibility mechanics, quorum, appeals, and pauses are defined in the governance policy before the first vote.</p>
    <p class="u-18"><a class="u-19" href="/policies/assembly-governance-participation/">Read the draft governance policy (POL-006)</a> — public review draft, not adopted.</p>
  </div>
</section>

